Subject: [PATCH v1 0/2] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K3L6XX sensor driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Samsung S5K3L6XX is a 13MP CMOS image sensor connected over a 4-lane
MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY bus. It is the ultra-wide camera of the Samsung Galaxy
A52 4G (a52q, SM7125).

This series adds a device tree binding and a V4L2 sub-device driver for
it. The driver is based on the S5K3L6XX driver by Martin Kepplinger and
Dorota Czaplejewicz (Purism SPC), reworked onto the v4l2-cci accessors
with register tables decoded from the vendor CamX sensor module. A
4000x3000 mode and a 2x2-binned 2000x1500 mode at 30 fps are supported.

Tested on the Galaxy A52 with libcamera (simple pipeline, camss) on a
downstream 6.14 kernel; the register tables are unchanged since.

